{"created": "2026-10-22T07:16:58.469416+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-22T07:16:59.653589+00:00", "id": 23554628, "conceptrecid": "23522054", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23554628", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23522054", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23554628", "metadata": {"title": "Bounds for the weak type (1,1) constant of the centred maximal operator over squares", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23554628", "publication_date": "2026-10-22", "description": "<p>Let c<sub>2</sub> be the best constant in the weak type (1,1) inequality for the centred Hardy\u2013Littlewood maximal operator over axis-parallel squares in the plane. The covering argument gives c<sub>2</sub> \u2264 4, and Lin proved c<sub>2</sub> &lt; 3.879, with a proof formalized in Lean. We prove c<sub>2</sub> \u2264 3.59123, improving the bound c<sub>2</sub> &lt; 3.615749 that Lin obtained with a kernel of the type described below. The proof uses a comparison principle of Lin, in coordinates (u, v) in which squares become diamonds: if an even, nonnegative, integrable kernel K is at least 1 on the diamond |u| + |v| \u2264 1 and A<sub>\u03b1</sub>K \u2265 0 away from the origin, where A<sub>\u03b1</sub> = \u2212|\u2202<sub>u</sub>|<sup>\u03b1</sup> \u2212 |\u2202<sub>v</sub>|<sup>\u03b1</sup> and 0 &lt; \u03b1 &lt; 2, then c<sub>2</sub> is at most half the integral of K. We prove this principle in detail, following Lin, and give closed forms for A<sub>\u03b1</sub> applied to cubic B-splines and to (|u| + |v|)<sup>\u2212\u03b1</sup>. With these, A<sub>\u03b1</sub>K is explicit for kernels made of a truncation of (|u| + |v|)<sup>\u2212\u03b1</sup> and finitely many tensor products of cubic B-splines. We exhibit such a kernel for \u03b1 = 47/40 with B-spline spacing 1/32, and two independent programs verify its properties in interval arithmetic. We also prove c<sub>2</sub> \u2265 1.7027237335, improving Lin's lower bound c<sub>2</sub> \u2265 1.6855. The proof changes the parameters of Lin's periodic lattice of point masses slightly and adds 48 small atoms to each period cell, on horizontal segments of six equal atoms; a program in exact rational arithmetic computes the area of a part of the superlevel set of the maximal function of this measure. Both bounds are also proved in Lean, with the numerical checks evaluated by the Lean kernel.</p>\n<p>The certificates of both bounds, their verification programs, the Lean proofs of both bounds, the search programs and the logs are archived at <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23554629\">doi:10.5281/zenodo.23554629</a>. They are also available at <a href=\"https://github.com/tejasvi/square-maximal-weak-type-v4\">github.com/tejasvi/square-maximal-weak-type-v4</a>.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Tomar, Tejasvi Singh", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0000-0003-4668-3639"}], "keywords": ["Hardy-Littlewood maximal function", "weak type (1,1)", "best constants", "fractional Laplacian", "partial balayage", "computer-assisted proof", "formal verification", "Lean 4"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.23554629", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "resource_type": "dataset", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "4", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 3, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23522054"}}]}}, "title": "Bounds for the weak type (1,1) constant of the centred maximal operator over squares", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23554628", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23554628", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23554628?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23554628", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23554628", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23554628", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23554628/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23522054", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23522054", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23522054", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23522054", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23554628/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23554628/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23554628/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23554628/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23554628:square-maximal-weak-type.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23554628:square-maximal-weak-type.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23554628:square-maximal-weak-type.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23554628:square-maximal-weak-type.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23554628:square-maximal-weak-type.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23554628:square-maximal-weak-type.pdf/full/%5E1200,/0/default.jpg"}, "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23554628/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23554628/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23554628/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23554628/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23554628/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23554628/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23554628/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23554628/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23554628/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23554628/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23554628/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/2